    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and the full suite passes with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership-level change in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`.\n\n**What changed in `getMembershipLevel()`:**\n- Kept the existing positive factors: base `1`, `+1` for a present email, `+1` for `namesakeCount == 0`.\n- Added the household factor: `+1` when the derived `householdSize` is 3 or more \u2014 this is what makes level 4 reachable.\n- Gated level 4 behind tenure: if the computed level reaches 4 but the owner's tenure is not more than 365 days, it is capped back to 3.\n\n**New helper `getTenureDays()`** computes whole days from `registrationDate` to today via `ChronoUnit.DAYS` (added the import), returning 0 when the date is absent or in the future.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` defaults to today (tenure \u2248 0), it can never exceed level 3 \u2014 so the maximal new-owner case (email + `namesakeCount` 0 + 3-member household, which sums to 4) is capped to 3, exactly as the spec and the new `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` require. Level 4 becomes reachable only once an established member's tenure passes 365 days.\n\nI also updated the method's Javadoc to document the household factor and the tenure requirement.",
