    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this entity:\n\n- **Logic lives in the right unit.** Membership-level derivation already belonged on the `Owner` model entity; the new tenure rule is added alongside the existing email/namesake rules, exactly where a maintainer would look for it.\n- **Good extraction.** The tenure computation is pulled into a well-named, single-purpose private helper `getTenureDays()` with its own javadoc documenting the null/future-date behavior, rather than inlined into `getMembershipLevel()`. That keeps the level method readable.\n- **No duplication or catch-all growth.** The method isn't accreting unrelated responsibility; it's still just \"compute the level,\" and the helper does one thing.\n- **Consistent with the prior idiom.** Expressing the tenure requirement as a guard that caps the level back to 3 mirrors the original `Math.min(level, 3)` capping style, and the household-size increment is needed for the spec's level-3 example to hold, so its addition is coherent rather than scope creep.\n- **Docs kept in sync.** The javadoc was rewritten to match the new behavior; the small overlap between the javadoc and the inline `// Level 4 is reserved...` comment is minor and not worth churning.",
